<title>PERU: BHP TO INVEST $150 MLN IN PERU COPPER PLANT.</title>
<headline>BHP TO INVEST $150 MLN IN PERU COPPER PLANT.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia's The Broken Hill Pty Co Ltd (BHP) plans to invest $150 million in a new copper plant in Peru, the government announced Friday in its official daily El Peruano.</p>
<p>BHP executives informed President Alberto Fujimori of its planned investment in a meeting at Government Palace late Thursday, according to El Peruano, which gave no details about the plant.</p>
<p>BHP is represented by the local firm Tintaya-Peru, El Peruano added.</p>
